            "Matching NOT performed for history of breast cancer, comorbidity index, screening frequency, or weight trajectory",
            "Matched event rates: GLP-1 247/15,264 (1.62%) vs Control 353/15,264 (2.31%)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Inappropriate BMI metric matching",
          "mechanism": "Matching on lifetime maximum BMI rather than baseline BMI at index date obscures active weight trajectories and residual adiposity confounding.",
          "evidence": ["Matching criterion explicitly specified as 'максимальный BMI'"]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "name": "Measurement of the exposure",
      "risk": "very_high",
      "direction": "away_from_null",
      "direction_justification": "Defining exposure as any prior/current prescription without duration, dose, or washout introduces immortal time and prevalent user biases, inflating the apparent protective effect (OR 0.649 full cohort, OR 0.695 matched).",
      "threatens_conclusions": true,
      "findings": [
        {
          "title": "Immortal time and prevalent user bias",
          "mechanism": "Patients had to survive and remain cancer-free long enough to receive a prescription prior to the cut-off date without requiring minimum exposure duration or new-user design.",
